From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: -read_latency is -register_read_address
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The option registers each read port's address: the decoders and read
trees come after the flop, and the data follows a cycle after the
address. -read_latency read as a register on the data, a different
circuit. 0 and 1 only; more than one cycle stops with RAM-0071.

Tested: src/ram/test/register_read_address_asap7.tcl,
src/ram/test/option_errors_asap7.tcl.

Commit 19 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
